          <circle class='human-point' cx='365' cy='98' r='9'></circle>
          <text x='48' y='203'>STIFF · 0</text><text x='312' y='203'>1 · COMPLIANT</text>
          <text x='52' y='49'>MOTION</text><text x='300' y='84'>Fext</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class='chapter safety-chapter' data-reveal>
      <div class='chapter-copy'>
        <span class='chapter-number'>02 / SAFETY</span>
        <h3>Can flexibility keep hard guarantees?</h3>
        <p>
          A second-order QP keeps joint, velocity, torque, and collision constraints strict—even
          while external forces reshape the motion.
        </p>
        <span class='chapter-detail'>COMPLIANCE INSIDE · CONSTRAINTS OUTSIDE</span>
      </div>
      <div class='chapter-figure safety-figure' aria-hidden='true'>
        <span class='figure-label'>FEASIBLE MOTION SPACE</span>
