          <path class='trajectory' d='M89 149C135 121 165 155 211 118S284 56 346 75'></path>
          <circle class='trajectory-point' cx='211' cy='118' r='10'></circle>
          <path class='limit' d='M53 99L98 43M333 55L376 126'></path>
          <text x='175' y='108'>QP</text><text x='69' y='34'>JOINT LIMIT</text><text x='296' y='44'
            >COLLISION</text
          >
        </svg>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class='chapter' data-reveal>
      <div class='chapter-copy'>
        <span class='chapter-number'>03 / OPEN QUESTION</span>
        <h3>How will people interpret the response?</h3>
        <p>
          This is an emerging direction: moving beyond controller performance to investigate how
          people perceive, anticipate, and physically guide robot behavior.
        </p>
        <span class='chapter-detail'>NEXT DIRECTION · PERCEPTION · HUMAN GUIDANCE</span>
      </div>
      <div class='chapter-figure experience-figure' aria-hidden='true'>
        <span class='figure-label'>SHARED SIGNAL</span>
